1. Server-side authentication verification in page component and API routes
2. Admin role checked server-side with 404 response for non-admins (prevents enumeration)
3. Service role key only used in server-side admin client, never exposed to client
4. All database queries use bound parameters via Supabase client
5. RLS policies enforce authorization at database level
6. API route validates input with Zod schema
7. Structured logging with redacted sensitive fields
8. Self-demotion prevention for admins
9. Rate limiting should be added at infrastructure level (not shown)
